        ]
      ],
      "id": "wamyb0r"
    },
    {
      "id": "basob4y",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Money Bills</li><li>Constitutional Amendment Bills</li></ul>",
        "Money Bills",
        "Constitutional Amendment Bills"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qcu85he",
      "content": "Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "4znokff",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Dowry Prohibition Bill</li><li>Banking Service Commission Bill</li></ul>",
        "Dowry Prohibition Bill",
        "Banking Service Commission Bill"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m8jszp9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "POWERS AND FUNCTIONS OF PARLIAMENT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a2vi7ye",
      "content": "Legislative Powers:"
    },
    {
      "id": "bpqt6nb",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Makes laws on Union and Concurrent List</li></ul>",
        "Makes laws on Union and Concurrent List"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "exdbzl6",
      "content": "Executive Powers:"
    },
    {
      "id": "c0z0rus",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Controls Council of Ministers</li><li>No-confidence motion</li></ul>",
        "Controls Council of Ministers",
        "No-confidence motion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9qhg0bp",
      "content": "Financial Powers:"
    },
    {
      "id": "9jx2zbn",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Budget approval</li><li>Taxation</li></ul>",
        "Budget approval",
        "Taxation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ho14eg2",
      "content": "Judicial Powers:"
    },
    {
      "id": "2yqs9iz",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Impeachment of President</li><li>Removal of judges</li></ul>",
        "Impeachment of President",
        "Removal of judges"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "krs9gde",
      "content": "Electoral Powers:"
    },
    {
      "id": "rnwaze3",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Election of President and Vice-President</li></ul>",
        "Election of President and Vice-President"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5vah5d5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PARLIAMENTARY PRIVILEGES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4pbgggb",
      "content": "Parliamentary privileges ensure smooth functioning. Includes:"
    },
    {
      "id": "fmi0pcj",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Freedom of speech</li><li>Freedom from arrest</li><li>Right to publish proceedings</li></ul>",
        "Freedom of speech",
        "Freedom from arrest",
        "Right to publish proceedings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bub6syr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PARLIAMENTARY COMMITTEES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ihox729",
      "content": "Types:"
    },
    {
      "id": "5a4owpi",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Standing Committees</li><li>Ad-hoc Committees</li></ul>",
        "Standing Committees",
        "Ad-hoc Committees"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qc6jlva",
      "content": "Functions:"
    },
    {
      "id": "nu0btii",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Examine bills</li><li>Scrutinize expenditure</li><li>Improve legislative efficiency</li></ul>",
        "Examine bills",
        "Scrutinize expenditure",
        "Improve legislative efficiency"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Rajya Sabha holds exclusive powers under Article 249 (State List legislation) and Article 312 (Creation of All India Services).",
        "The decision of the Lok Sabha Speaker on whether a bill is a Money Bill is final.",
        "The President is an integral part of Parliament under Article 79, despite not being a member of either House.",
        "Disqualification decisions under the Anti-Defection Law by the Presiding Officer are subject to judicial review."
      ],
      "id": "hr4r370"
    },
    {
      "id": "f17hskp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "DISQUALIFICATION OF MEMBERS"
    },
